{"baseRefName":"fix/audit-hardening","baseRefOid":"f4456ebf65eddbb7d3bf4d3a0f5136e9a44d7ebb","body":"## Summary\nStacked on #539. Three destructive-path audit findings in the install/uninstall lifecycle:\n\n- **`cleanupOldBinary` swept every `*.old` in the binary's dir** — the only aside self-replace writes is `<binPath>.old`. Foreign files sharing the suffix (`logs.txt.old` rotations, user backups) were deleted on every launch whenever the binary dir doubled as a working dir. Now removes the exact aside only.\n- **`nativeUninstall` wiped foreign files in `transactions/`** — entries are now limited to the `<id>.json` namespace the installer writes, and the dir is only removed once nothing foreign remains. Preserving residue is not a lifecycle failure, so the manifest still unlinks.\n- **`void cleanupOldVersions(layout)` floated a rejection-capable promise** — an unexpected throw inside (lock-content read, `process.kill` edge) became an unhandled rejection on a background path. Added the `.catch` that `main.ts`'s call site already had.\n\n#### Test plan\n- [x] New regression: foreign `*.old` survives cleanup; `<bin>.old` removed\n- [x] New regression: foreign file in `transactions/` survives; dir preserved; manifest still removed; no `failed` entries\n- [x] Full affected gate: 26 tasks, 5948 unit + 296 integration, 0 fail\n- [x] Anti-slop baseline: 4407, zero drift","files":[{"path":"apps/cli/src/services/update/native-installer/install-latest.ts","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/cli/src/services/update/native-installer/native-uninstall.ts","additions":9,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/cli/src/services/update/self-replace.ts","additions":5,"deletions":9,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/cli/test/unit/self-replace.test.ts","additions":15,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/cli/test/unit/services/update/native-installer/native-uninstall.test.ts","additions":20,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIF